Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.74,0:00:59.78,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Who is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.78,0:01:01.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's me, Miss Anna.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.48,0:01:04.13,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to bother you so late.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.81,0:01:07.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I have something important \Nto discuss with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.23,0:01:21.28,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.56,0:03:33.47,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Don't be nervous, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.47,0:03:34.81,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I mean you no harm.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.73,0:03:36.40,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Who...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.27,0:03:38.31,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Who are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.70,0:03:42.34,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,The Sacred Mountain and Magic Eye?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.26,0:03:48.49,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I didn't expect you to be such \Na learned man, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.81,0:03:55.18,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,You're a witch?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:56.18,0:03:57.00,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.55,0:03:59.81,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You may call me Nightingale.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.81,0:04:00.94,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Nightingale...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.86,0:04:03.81,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Why have you come here?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.34,0:04:08.81,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,First, I must thank you, Roland Wimbledon.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.81,0:04:09.86,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Thank me?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.36,0:04:11.31,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,For what?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.77,0:04:13.32,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,For Anna and Nana.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.32,0:04:16.31,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,You know about Anna and Nana?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.31,0:04:18.32,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I heard a witch had been captured here,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.32,0:04:19.96,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,so I came to rescue her.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.96,0:04:23.53,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,To my surprise, you didn't \Nexecute the girl named Anna.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.53,0:04:27.47,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I spent the next week observing Nana \Nand learned about her as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.47,0:04:30.25,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Although I don't know why \Nyou hold no ill will toward witches,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.25,0:04:33.47,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I still want to thank you on behalf of \Nthe Witch Cooperation Association.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.47,0:04:37.26,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Are you saying you've been \Nlurking by my side for a whole week?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.26,0:04:39.50,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,It's so tiring talking like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.50,0:04:41.52,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Shouldn't you invite a lady to sit down?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.10,0:04:58.98,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,What, do I look that terrifying?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.26,0:05:09.77,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Will you answer my question now?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.87,0:05:13.77,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You're really not afraid of me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.14,0:05:19.04,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I can see the fear of \Nwitches in people's eyes,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.77,0:05:21.31,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,but in yours,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.89,0:05:23.38,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I see only curiosity.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.32,0:05:26.23,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I arrived here a week ago
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.74,0:05:29.38,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,and have been lurking \Nby your side ever since.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.38,0:05:31.77,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I've seen everything you've done.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.22,0:05:35.77,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,So, why have you revealed yourself now?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.56,0:05:39.83,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Just now, your head maid came in
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.83,0:05:41.77,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,to pour you a glass of \Nred wine before bed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.44,0:05:45.67,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Then she added a little \Nsomething extra to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.19,0:05:47.91,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,You...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.66,0:05:49.93,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,You mean Tyre?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.70,0:05:52.27,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,She poisoned my wine?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.22,0:05:57.27,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,It seems your harem isn't entirely safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.11,0:06:01.77,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,I've never touched her.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.30,0:06:08.83,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,So, you saved me.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.54,0:06:11.27,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,I owe you my thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.33,0:06:13.69,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,It's nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.80,0:06:16.25,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,A life for a life.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.25,0:06:17.49,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You saved Anna,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.49,0:06:19.27,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,so I helped you get rid of a traitor.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.58,0:06:22.26,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Now we're even.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.12,0:06:30.27,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I need to take Anna and \NNana away from here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.40,0:06:32.74,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,You want to take them away?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.74,0:06:33.27,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.60,0:06:34.80,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Where to?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.80,0:06:36.46,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Back to the Witch Cooperation Association.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.46,0:06:38.13,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,That's where witches truly belong.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:38.13,0:06:38.94,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Why?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.06,0:06:41.54,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Only in the Witch Cooperation Association
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.08,0:06:43.95,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,can witches live without discrimination,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.95,0:06:45.69,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,without persecution,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.69,0:06:47.49,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,and without having to hide themselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.49,0:06:49.43,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,They won't be persecuted here either.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.43,0:06:52.25,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,I've given them equal \Ncontracts and high salaries.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.25,0:06:53.85,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,You can see that they're doing well here.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.85,0:06:55.81,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You've done a lot for the witches,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.46,0:06:58.85,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,but there's one thing you can't do.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.12,0:07:02.85,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You can't lead them... \Nto the Holy Mountain.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.49,0:07:04.27,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,The Holy Mountain?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.27,0:07:05.20,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.97,0:07:08.97,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Only there can witches find eternal peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.38,0:07:12.97,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,My men previously discovered traces \Nof witches in the northern mountains.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.31,0:07:16.36,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Are you trying to find the Holy Mountain \Nin the Impassable Mountain Range?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.36,0:07:17.35,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,No comment.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.79,0:07:24.32,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,In that case, \Nthere's no way I can allow it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.32,0:07:26.48,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,The Months of Demons begin in two months.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.48,0:07:29.87,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,The mountains will be full \Nof snow and demonic beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.87,0:07:32.31,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,I won't let Anna and Nana\Ntake such a risk.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.29,0:07:34.58,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,How about this?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.58,0:07:36.33,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,You can find the Holy \NMountain at any time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.33,0:07:38.72,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Why don't you all come to \NBorder Town for the winter?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.72,0:07:41.51,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,You can continue your \Nsearch after the winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.51,0:07:43.23,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You're suggesting
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.65,0:07:46.39,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,we bring the entire Witch Cooperation\NAssociation to Border Town?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.09,0:07:48.66,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,How amusing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.66,0:07:49.93,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,That's impossible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.33,0:07:52.46,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Your Highness, even if you're \Nnot afraid of witches,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.46,0:07:54.25,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,there are far too many who are.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.78,0:07:56.08,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Once witches are exposed,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.08,0:07:58.32,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,the Church will come knocking in no time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.32,0:08:00.14,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Why would you take such a huge risk
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.14,0:08:01.52,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,rather than let them leave?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.84,0:08:04.77,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Because... they're very important to me.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.23,0:08:06.44,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,In that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.09,0:08:09.85,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,you surely don't want Anna's \Nlife to be in danger, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.03,0:08:13.14,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Are you saying Anna's life is in danger?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.14,0:08:16.43,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Yes. That's why I have to take her away.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.98,0:08:18.81,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Anna is about to come of age.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.81,0:08:22.49,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,The Day of Adulthood is the first \Nmajor ordeal every witch must face.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.49,0:08:25.36,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Most witches awaken during \Nthe Months of Demons,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:25.36,0:08:28.04,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,which is said to be when \Nthe Gates of Hell open.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.04,0:08:30.62,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Coming of age marks a \Nturning point for witches.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.62,0:08:32.82,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Girls who have not \Nawakened by the age of 18
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.82,0:08:34.61,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,will most likely never become witches.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.61,0:08:36.42,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,But for those who awaken before 18,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.42,0:08:38.35,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,every year on the anniversary \Nof their awakening,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.35,0:08:40.90,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,they suffer the torment \Nof demonic possession.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.90,0:08:44.13,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Every blood vessel and sinew \Naches with unbearable pain.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.72,0:08:47.62,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,In the end, blood seeps from their skin,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.62,0:08:49.73,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,and their eyeballs bulge \Nfrom their sockets.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.73,0:08:50.84,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,If they can endure it,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.84,0:08:53.86,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,their bodies will slowly recover \Nafter four or five days of rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.86,0:08:57.34,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,But those who can't \Nhold on will die in agony,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.34,0:08:59.28,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,their deaths horrific to behold.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.91,0:09:03.25,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Blood mixed with internal organs \Nbursts from every orifice.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.25,0:09:06.05,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Upon contact with air, \Nit turns into black mist.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.05,0:09:09.31,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Finally, when everything that \Ncan be expelled is gone,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.31,0:09:12.80,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,only a layer of charred black \Nskin remains on the ground.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.53,0:09:16.32,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Many witches die on the \Nday they come of age.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.44,0:09:21.10,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,This is the evidence for why we are \Nseen as the incarnation of the Devil.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.60,0:09:24.60,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Anna is about to come of age.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.41,0:09:28.03,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,In the Witch Cooperation Association, \Nwe know how to care for her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.03,0:09:30.03,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Her chances of survival are much higher.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:30.03,0:09:33.13,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,And the Holy Mountain will \Nbring us eternal peace.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.94,0:09:37.17,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Therefore, I must take Anna and Nana away.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.17,0:09:40.60,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Perhaps they are indispensable \Nto Your Highness's grand plans,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.60,0:09:44.24,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,but I still hope you can \Ngive them a chance to live.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.98,0:09:49.92,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.52,0:09:53.77,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,In that case, I'll let you take them.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.77,0:09:55.03,Flashback,Roland,0,0,0,,I'll take you to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.90,0:09:58.85,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Thank you for your understanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.66,0:10:02.45,Flashback,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I knew I hadn't misjudged you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.86,0:10:48.89,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Who is it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.16,0:10:51.41,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It's me, Miss Anna.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:52.39,0:10:54.34,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'm sorry to bother you so late.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.34,0:10:56.92,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I have something important \Nto discuss with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.29,0:11:05.36,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.50,0:11:08.33,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I understand everything you've said.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.33,0:11:11.47,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Thank you, Nightingale, \Nfor coming to save me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.18,0:11:14.68,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,But I'm not leaving.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.53,0:11:19.22,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Wh-What did you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.22,0:11:21.22,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I said, I want to stay here.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.63,0:11:25.56,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Anna, you still don't understand how \Nterrible the demonic possession can be.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.56,0:11:27.64,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Your magic is nearing maturity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.64,0:11:29.35,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Once it's affected by \Nthe Months of Demons...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.35,0:11:30.35,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I don't care.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.35,0:11:32.33,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,The demonic possession won't kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.33,0:11:33.35,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I will overcome it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:33.99,0:11:35.86,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I just want to stay by \NHis Highness's side.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.20,0:11:45.35,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.65,0:11:48.27,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,In that case, I'll stay here for now, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:48.27,0:11:49.11,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.11,0:11:50.18,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.18,0:11:51.11,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Didn't you want to bring
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.11,0:11:53.37,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,the entire Witch Cooperation\NAssociation to Border Town?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.86,0:11:56.08,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I have experience.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:56.08,0:11:59.08,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,On the Day of Adulthood, \NI can at least be of some help.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.70,0:12:02.30,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,And if you don't make it through,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.30,0:12:04.27,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I also have experience \Nhandling the aftermath.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.27,0:12:06.85,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,I will definitely make it through.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.07,0:12:13.90,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I'll be in your care for a while, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.49,0:12:30.37,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Well, I'll be going now.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:30.37,0:12:31.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Get some rest.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.53,0:12:38.35,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.23,0:13:17.59,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Good morning, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.50,0:13:20.85,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Good morning, Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.32,0:13:22.60,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Did something happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.60,0:13:24.99,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your head maid, Tyre, died last night.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.99,0:13:27.13,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Huh? What happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.13,0:13:30.47,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,This morning, the guards found \Nshe had fallen from her room's balcony.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.47,0:13:32.93,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,There were no signs of a struggle, \Nand no outsiders had entered,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.93,0:13:36.58,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,so... it was likely an accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.58,0:13:38.14,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Oh. Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.85,0:13:40.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Give her a proper burial.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.89,0:13:42.14,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.14,0:13:45.01,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Go ahead. I'll head to the \Nregular meeting after breakfast.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.01,0:13:46.42,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Wait for me in the office.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:46.42,0:13:47.57,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.96,0:13:53.52,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Good morning, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:07.81,0:14:09.06,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You did it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.06,0:14:11.44,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Since I'll be imposing for \Na few days, Your Highness,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.44,0:14:13.38,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,it's only natural that \NI help relieve your worries.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.38,0:14:15.14,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Do you know who sent her?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.97,0:14:20.52,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Actually, I didn't kill her.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.52,0:14:22.03,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,She had poison hidden in her tooth.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.03,0:14:23.71,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,The moment she saw me, she killed herself.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.71,0:14:25.47,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I had no choice but to make \Nit look like an accident.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.47,0:14:29.39,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,It seems someone kidnapped her sister \Nas a hostage and sent her to kill me.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.42,0:14:32.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Probably one of my siblings.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.47,0:14:38.73,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Family relations among the nobility \Nhave always been like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.98,0:14:42.10,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Anyway, you should go to your meeting now.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.10,0:14:43.44,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Don't keep them waiting.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.23,0:14:48.04,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,But I haven't had...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.11,0:15:03.31,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.31,0:15:06.06,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Have you been feeling \Ntired these past few days?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.06,0:15:07.76,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Ah, it's nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.76,0:15:09.00,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Just a bit hungry.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.00,0:15:11.14,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Hungry? But Your Highness, you just—
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.14,0:15:13.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I'm fine. All right, \Nlet's begin the meeting.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.77,0:15:14.81,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Very well, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.52,0:15:17.86,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Regarding this ore trade with Willow Town,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.86,0:15:20.25,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,since we sold it at 50% \Nof the market price,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.25,0:15:22.25,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,we only made a profit of 200 gold royals.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.25,0:15:25.40,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,After deducting expenses for food \Nand the city wall construction,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.40,0:15:27.06,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,we have 90 left.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.06,0:15:30.22,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Although it's still tight, we should \Nbe able to get through the winter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.22,0:15:33.12,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,However, given your announcement \Nyesterday about forming a militia,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.12,0:15:36.68,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,that expense will have to come \Nout of your personal treasury.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.68,0:15:39.89,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Understood. Carter, how goes \Nthe militia recruitment?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.89,0:15:42.64,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,There are many applicants.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.64,0:15:45.46,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,The planned squad of \N100 men is almost full.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.46,0:15:49.16,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,However, the training and command \Nof this unit are highly problematic.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.16,0:15:52.54,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,We can't expect a bunch of workers and \Nfarmers to fend off demonic beasts.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.54,0:15:54.18,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,They don't even know how to hold a sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.18,0:15:55.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What is your suggestion?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.50,0:15:56.87,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,We need knights.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.87,0:15:59.66,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I know Your Highness may not \Ncare for the local nobles,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.66,0:16:04.08,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,but I still believe we should seek the \Nsupport of Baron Boris and the knights.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.08,0:16:06.63,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Please allow me to go \Nmeet with Baron Boris.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.63,0:16:08.62,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,This concerns the safety of Border Town.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.62,0:16:11.70,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I believe we have a chance \Nto rally them to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:14.49,0:16:15.86,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I understand, Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.50,0:16:18.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Go and arrange a meeting with Baron Boris.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.50,0:16:20.72,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Tell him I will visit tomorrow morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.15,0:16:22.32,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Yes, Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.16,0:16:24.22,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Thank you for understanding.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.11,0:16:39.56,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, do you think \NBaron Boris will help us?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.18,0:16:41.61,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,There's a 90% chance he won't.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:41.61,0:16:43.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter is a loyal knight.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.08,0:16:46.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I agreed to go to appease him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.56,0:16:50.67,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Carter may be too naive \Nwhen it comes to politics,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:50.67,0:16:53.56,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,but militarily, he's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.94,0:16:57.07,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,Your Highness, your queen \Nhas already been captured,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.07,0:16:58.89,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,the knight is surrounded,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.89,0:17:00.96,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,and the bishop cannot hold the line alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.96,0:17:03.79,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,If the last remaining pawns get captured,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.79,0:17:06.30,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,what do you have left to win with?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:07.82,0:17:10.81,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You're too focused on the decoys, Barov.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.55,0:17:13.62,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,What will truly help me achieve victory
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.04,0:17:20.43,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,are these people who push forward \Nwith all their strength to the very end.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:20.43,0:17:24.36,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,But even if you have the \Npeople's support now,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.36,0:17:28.31,Main,Barov,0,0,0,,they have no combat experience \Nand they're unarmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.47,0:17:31.59,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,They will receive thorough training.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.17,0:17:33.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And also,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.18,0:17:36.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,they won't be fighting unarmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.28,0:17:42.75,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Okay, now, like this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.75,0:17:44.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,See the gap in the middle \Nof the iron pipe?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.70,0:17:45.50,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.50,0:17:48.12,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Now concentrate the flame as much \Nas possible on a single point,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.12,0:17:49.73,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,the thinner the better.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.73,0:17:52.77,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Slowly burn along this gap.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.41,0:17:54.08,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.77,0:18:02.74,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Draw it in a little more.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:02.74,0:18:05.27,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Concentrate all the heat \Nonto your fingertip.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.48,0:18:08.70,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Concentrate, concentrate a bit more.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.46,0:18:10.65,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,That's right, just like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.47,0:18:12.18,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Slowly...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.64,0:18:16.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Follow the gap.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.02,0:18:17.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Yes, burn through.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.10,0:18:20.75,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,A little slower. Steady, steady.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.38,0:18:24.64,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You did it!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.83,0:18:31.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Anna.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.39,0:18:33.22,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.06,0:18:38.50,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Look, Anna.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.38,0:18:41.22,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This is what we've \Nachieved this afternoon,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.02,0:18:42.84,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,all thanks to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.84,0:18:45.47,Main,Anna,0,0,0,,Your Highness, what is this exactly?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.90,0:18:48.47,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You'll find out soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.19,0:18:53.07,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This thing... will open \Nthe door to a new era.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:04.73,0:19:06.97,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Good evening, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.54,0:19:09.68,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Why are you acting like a stalker?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.97,0:19:13.00,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You're just too intriguing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.00,0:19:14.82,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Besides, since I'm staying,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.82,0:19:16.85,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I need to protect you and Anna.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.85,0:19:18.64,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,What if there's another assassin?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.59,0:19:20.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,So I'm supposed to thank you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.75,0:19:22.92,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You're welcome.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.92,0:19:25.43,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,Besides, I've already received my reward.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:26.72,0:19:29.56,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,This is what you had \NAnna make today, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.24,0:19:31.80,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,You took that from my office.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.34,0:19:36.00,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I just thought it might be useful.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:36.00,0:19:38.64,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,There are other fire users in the \NWitch Cooperation Association.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:39.46,0:19:40.76,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Go ahead and keep it.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.76,0:19:42.35,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I can draw another one.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:42.35,0:19:44.10,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,You treat Anna really well,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.42,0:19:45.75,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,and she trusts you a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.10,0:19:49.06,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,I've long forgotten
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.51,0:19:51.76,Main,Nightingale,0,0,0,,what it feels like to \Ntrust and be trusted.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.06,0:20:05.62,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Baron Boris's house is on the \Nwesternmost part of town.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.62,0:20:07.60,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,You'll recognize it the moment you see it.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.60,0:20:11.34,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,In Border Town, his house \Nis practically a mansion.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.34,0:20:12.02,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.63,0:20:14.72,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,They say he hired an \Narchitect from Graycastle
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.72,0:20:17.30,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,and used the finest timber and stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.30,0:20:19.47,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,It wouldn't look out of \Nplace even in Graycastle.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.31,0:20:24.59,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,He brags to everyone that his \Nhouse is worth 150 gold royals.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.98,0:20:27.97,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Well, I'll have to see it for myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.60,0:20:53.45,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Your Highness, your courage and resolve \Nto hold Border Town are truly admirable.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:53.45,0:20:57.05,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,It is our honor that you thought \Nof us in your time of need.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.05,0:21:00.38,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,May I ask what exactly \NYour Highness needs us to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.87,0:21:02.61,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,The militia currently lacks instructors,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.61,0:21:05.53,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,essential weapons, \Nand experienced fighters.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.53,0:21:07.99,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I hope you will answer my call
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.99,0:21:10.93,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,and lead your knights to help \Ndefend Border Town together.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.30,0:21:13.37,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.37,0:21:16.59,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Since Your Highness personally \Ncame to ask us for help,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:16.59,0:21:18.93,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,it is only right that we do our duty.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.93,0:21:22.15,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,However, it's truly unfortunate.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.82,0:21:31.06,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,My knights have just returned \Nfrom a hunt and are exhausted.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.06,0:21:34.33,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,Besides, fighting demonic \Nbeasts is extremely dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.33,0:21:36.80,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,I cannot send them to their deaths.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.39,0:21:41.41,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,I assume raising a militia \Nalso requires funds.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.41,0:21:44.51,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,So to show our support,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.51,0:21:47.18,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,we've discussed and decided to
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.18,0:21:50.89,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,jointly contribute some \Nfunds toward your efforts.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.89,0:21:53.53,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,As a token of our goodwill,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.53,0:21:56.47,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,please accept this offer, Your Highness.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.53,0:21:56.47,Italics - Top,Carter,0,0,0,,One... One gold royal?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.87,0:21:58.02,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,You—
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.02,0:21:58.98,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Carter.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.43,0:22:03.62,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I accept your kind offer.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.62,0:22:04.47,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.47,0:22:07.47,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Well then, we'll take our leave for today.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.20,0:22:09.99,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,My leg isn't what it used to be,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:09.99,0:22:11.64,Main,Boris,0,0,0,,so forgive me for not seeing you out.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:21.80,0:22:24.13,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,Your Highness, I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.13,0:22:26.01,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I've brought shame upon you.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.76,0:22:29.30,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,I knew they probably wouldn't help,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.30,0:22:31.65,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,but I never imagined they'd stoop so low.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.65,0:22:34.91,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,This is an insult to \Nthe loyalty of knights.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.91,0:22:39.29,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,Don't worry about it, Carter.\NI expected as much.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.29,0:22:42.58,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,At least this one gold royal will \Ncover a month's wages for Mr. Karl.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.58,0:22:44.58,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,And it also makes it clear that
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.58,0:22:46.57,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,if we want to establish ourselves here,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.57,0:22:48.49,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,we cannot rely on the nobles.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.43,0:22:53.10,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,B-But without the nobles and knights,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.10,0:22:55.14,Main,Carter,0,0,0,,how can we train that ragtag militia?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:02.07,0:23:03.59,Main,Roland,0,0,0,,I have my ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.10,0:23:08.40,Main - Top,CREDITS,0,0,0,,Translator: Henry Lin\NTimer: Henry Lin\NEditor: Zachary Carlysle\N QC: William Haggard
